<h1>Routly — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: 23 September 2026</p>

<p>Routly is a navigation app that provides turn-by-turn directions and rates the sharpness of corners on your route. This policy explains what the app does and does not do with your information. It is written to be read plainly, not as legal boilerplate.</p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Routly keeps your data on your device. It does not have accounts, does not run its own servers, and does not sell, share, or transmit your personal information to us or to any third party for advertising or analytics.</p>

<h2>Location</h2>
<p>Routly uses your device's location to show where you are, to give turn-by-turn navigation, to rate the corners on the road ahead, and to measure speed and acceleration during a drive. Location is processed on your device. With your permission, Routly can continue to use location in the background so that voice guidance keeps working while the screen is off or you are in another app.</p>
<p>Routing and map data are provided by Apple Maps (MapKit). When Routly requests a route or searches for a place, that request is handled by Apple under Apple's own privacy policy. Routly does not receive or store a separate copy of that data.</p>

<h2>Information you enter</h2>
<p>You may optionally add a driver profile — a name, a car, a country, and a photo. This is stored only on your device. It is not uploaded anywhere in this version of the app.</p>

<h2>Records kept on your device</h2>
<p>Routly saves your recent searches, your acceleration-run statistics, and your personal best times and top speeds. All of this is stored locally on your device and can be cleared at any time from the app's Settings.</p>

<h2>Purchases</h2>
<p>Routly Pro is an optional subscription sold through Apple's App Store. Payments and subscription management are handled entirely by Apple. Routly never sees your payment details. Apple's handling of purchases is covered by Apple's privacy policy.</p>

<h2>Data we collect about you</h2>
<p>None. Routly does not collect analytics, does not use tracking, and does not include third-party advertising or measurement software.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Routly is a general-audience navigation app and is not directed at children.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If a future version of Routly adds online features, such as a synced leaderboard, this policy will be updated to describe them before those features are released.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy or the app can be sent to <a href="mailto:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_EMAIL">REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_EMAIL</a>.</p>

